      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source before improving understandability.Now I have a clear picture. The test verifies that `truncate()` snaps the position down to the new size when the current position is beyond it, even when no actual resize occurs (truncate target equals current size). I'll improve readability with a clear Arrange/Act/Assert structure, named variables, and a concise explanation.The improved test compiled successfully (`COMPILE_OK`)."
